---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { classes } from '../../../styles';
---
<DocsLayout title="Motion and transforms" description="Transitions, animation, translate, rotate, scale, and skew."><header><p class={classes.eyebrow}>Utility reference</p><h1 class={classes.title}>Motion and transforms</h1><p class={classes.lead}>Transitions, animation, translate, rotate, scale, and skew.</p></header><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Classes</h2><p class={classes.copy}>transition-*, duration-*, delay-*, ease-*, animate-*, animation-duration-*, animation-delay-*, animation-ease-*, animation-iterations-*, animation-direction-*, animation-fill-*, animation-running, animation-paused, translate-x/y-*, rotate-*, scale-*, and skew-x/y-*.</p></section><section class={classes.section}><h2 class={classes.heading}>Animation longhands</h2><pre class={classes.code}><code>animate-spin animation-duration-500 animation-delay-[150ms]{`\n`}animation-ease-out animation-iterations-infinite animation-fill-both</code></pre><p class={classes.copy}>Animation longhands emit after animate-* so they override values in its shorthand. Numeric duration and delay values use milliseconds. Define --animation-duration-name or --animation-ease-name in @theme for named values.</p></section></DocsLayout>
